1
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,000
The Last Godfather is a comedy, crime, romance film directed by Shim Hyung-rae.

2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Young-goo the son of mafia boss Don Carini, is too
foolish to be part of the mafia elite.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
One day, Young-goo comes to his father and is trained
by Tony V to be his father's successor.

4
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
A few days later, Young-goo accidentally rescues Nancy, the only
daughter of Don Bonfante, the boss of a rival mafia family.

5
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
But Vinnie, an under-boss of the Bonfante family kidnapped her
and fabricates that Young-goo has taken her.

6
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Vinnie's behavior provokes an armed conflict between the two families.

7
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Young-gu, played by Shim Hyung-rae.

8
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Don Carini, played by Harvey Keitel.

9
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Tony V, played by Michael Rispoli.

10
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Vinnie, played by Jason Mewes.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Nancy Bonfante, played by Jocelin Donahue.

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Captain O'Brian, played by Blake Clark.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
The Last Godfather (Korean: 라스트 갓파더) is a 2010 mafia
comedy film directed by Shim Hyung-rae.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The film explores themes of new york city, mafia, godfather.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
